('abfd3b2c-f8a5-462b-bd4a-cdd1abe03c07', 'Side Step Pulldown', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this pulling exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '97791201', '97791201-Side-Step-Pulldown-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Side Step Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('abfd458f-64e7-4048-a020-a87ed6cb33af', 'Pulse Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '38031201', '38031201-Bodyweight-Pulse-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Pulse Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('abff7847-32a0-4bf9-8b6f-7a8fd9cc15fd', 'Pike Stand', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Pike Stand helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '94881201', '94881201-Pike-Stand-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Pike Stand. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Pike Stand', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac18848e-0f85-44f4-bd60-77c17ab8f003', 'Half Lotus Pulse', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your hips, the Half Lotus Pulse helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The adductors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '84891201', '84891201-Half-Lotus-Pulse-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Half Lotus Pulse. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 15, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pulse', 'Half Lotus Pulse', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac1eefb7-12e5-4891-9bb9-22fbf133dd05', 'Standing Calf Raise On A Stepbox (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted raising exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '92971201', '92971201-Bodyweight-Standing-Calf-Raise-on-a-Stepbox-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Standing Calf Raise On A Stepbox', 'calf_raise, seated_calf_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac244be2-b334-4761-a35f-1ef473ee5ed9', 'Superman - Around the World', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your chest working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '85541201', '85541201-Around-the-World-Superman-(VERSION-2)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Around The World Superman. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Around The World Superman', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac2653c4-ea93-43c2-a429-af3bb44a9935', 'Pulse Split Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Pulse Split Lunge is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '51971201', '51971201-Pulse-Split-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Pulse Split Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac2e4499-f3d6-4289-9d46-a14ce167d2ef', 'Forearm Push Forward', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pushing movement focusing on your rear delts. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '66891201', '66891201-Forearm-Push-Forward-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Forearm Push Forward. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your rear delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Forearm Push Forward', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac31ea3b-309d-4227-8cd2-d289b89c4046', 'Seated Foot Inversion (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted movement exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '67461201', '67461201-Cable-Seated-Foot-Inversion-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Foot Inversion. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Foot Inversion', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ac35641f-85b0-4fc9-9cab-9242d60e9e56', 'Bicep Curl - Single Arm (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Alternate Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '231201', '00231201-Barbell-Alternate-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Alternate Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl - Alternating', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('ac4da2e3-8322-4ded-b678-9a4842427369', 'Front Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '26391201', '26391201-Kettlebell-Front-Squat-(female)_thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Front Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'front_squat', 'Front Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('ac623a5a-82cb-437d-beeb-11d878f6a8eb', 'Overhead And Under Knee Clap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Overhead And Under Knee Clap builds reactive power and improves conditioning. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '81721201', '81721201-Overhead-and-Under-Knee-Clap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Overhead And Under Knee Clap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Overhead And Under Knee Clap', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac727fb1-b9df-4a79-9ea4-538cc0c506d6', 'Standing Overhead Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '23801201', '23801201-Dumbbell-Standing-Overhead-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Overhead Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 99, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_press', 'Standing Overhead Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ac89f43d-e3f1-444e-b9ca-426b6f2c99cf', 'Downward Dog Push Up (Against Wall)', 'Chest', 'Wall', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Downward Dog Push Up Against Wall provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '69861201', '69861201-Downward-Dog-Push-up-against-Wall-(male)_Plyometri.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Dog Push Up Against Wall', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ac92dbe4-fb5e-49c3-9b5d-eac2d33fbb99', 'Single Leg Split Squat With Low Box (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Single Leg Split Squat With Low Box is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '72391201', '72391201-Dumbbell-Single-Leg-Split-Squat-with-Low-Box_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 4. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 5. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Single Leg Split Squat With Low Box', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ac9ea07f-1ed3-4653-aab2-557e9fdce2da', 'Sliding Leg Bird Dog', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back","Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Sliding Leg Bird Dog is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Secondary activation of your glutes, abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '44161201', '44161201-Sliding-Leg-Bird-Dog_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sliding Leg Bird Dog. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Sliding Leg Bird Dog', 'dead_bug, plank, back_extension', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('accf36d9-e434-4274-9e98-74b566a153a4', 'Single Arm Bent Over Row (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell One Arm Bent Over Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your biceps, lats work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '641201', '00641201-Barbell-One-Arm-Bent-over-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell One Arm Bent Over Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bent_over_row', 'Single Arm Bent Over Row', 'cable_row, dumbbell_row, t_bar_row, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('acd8acaa-b95e-46c2-812f-46d72a3750ab', 'Bent Over Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, lats assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '2931201', '02931201-Dumbbell-Bent-Over-Row_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bent Over Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bent_over_row', 'Bent Over Row', 'cable_row, dumbbell_row, t_bar_row, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('acdc0671-4700-48d0-ae00-94a20bbd135d', 'Cross Over Reverse Fly (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'This dynamic flying movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '1541201', '01541201-Cable-Cross-over-Revers-Fly_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Cross Over Revers Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Cross Over Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('acf53939-ff23-495a-a3ba-a0b6429f221d', 'Front Plank With Arm And Leg Lift', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Front Plank With Arm And Leg Lift, focusing on your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '54661201', '54661201-Front-Plank-with-Arm-and-Leg-Lift-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. Include this in your core training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank With Arm And Leg Lift', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('acf54dcd-310c-47aa-a5a2-c597cdcf8338', 'Wrist Circles', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Wrist Circles strengthens your forearms and grip through a movement motion. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '43231201', '43231201-Wrist-Circles-(female)_Forearms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.146812+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wrist Circles. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_stretch', 'Wrist Circles', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad044631-7060-4afd-b667-52b00240d9b9', 'Single Arm Clean And Press (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint pressing movement. Your shoulders, legs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '82981201', '82981201-Dumbbell-Single-Arm-Clean-and-Press-(male)_Weightl.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Single Arm Clean And Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'clean', 'Single Arm Clean And Press', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ad08f2f3-10ee-4154-a19b-2306105bc4d1', 'Lying Prone W To Y', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '106941201', '106941201-Lying-Prone-W-to-Y-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie face down with your body in a straight line. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Prone W To Y. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Prone W To Y', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad0cc46e-27b0-4e6c-9794-00196893dfb0', 'Bike Crunch And Feet Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Bike Crunch And Feet Tap is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '78281201', '78281201-Bike-Crunch-and-Feet-Tap-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. Include this in your core training. Variation: Bike Crunch And Feet Tap.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Bike Crunch And Feet Tap', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad0d9eed-a240-454e-9f0b-d6e918126ece', 'Fly March', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Fly March builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '99001201', '99001201-Fly-March-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 2. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 3. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Fly March', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad0db933-b9ad-4410-b107-1499071b7071', 'Frog Reverse Hyperextension (On A Bench)', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Frog Reverse Hyperextension (on A Bench) is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. The hamstrings, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '31791201', '31791201-Frog-Reverse-Hyperextension-(on-a-bench)-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Frog Reverse Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad1524b4-ea32-4927-a7c2-5198f4a868f0', 'Push (Plate)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Plate Push is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic pushing movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '78821201', '78821201-Plate-Push-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Plate Push. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Plate Push', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad290868-ae24-4605-a2ff-cdf85c15274f', 'Standing Shoulder External Rotatio (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Resistance Band Standing Shoulder External Rotatio, a comprehensive movement exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '93941201', '93941201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Shoulder-External-Rotatio.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Shoulder External Rotatio. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Standing Shoulder External Rotatio', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('ad2c370c-6ca1-4c01-b349-9869b81fbd8b', 'Ring Archer Push Up (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Chest', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Ring Archer Push Up, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '75101201', '75101201-Ring-Archer-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Perfect for targeting your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Ring Archer Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('ad2cd37c-01d2-4501-ad59-18c32332a683', 'Stepback Oblique Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Stepback Oblique Twist builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '84601201', '84601201-Stepback-Oblique-Twist-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Stepback Oblique Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Stepback Oblique Twist', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad4172fb-0fa1-486e-93da-f002c11f12ab', 'Standing Hands Up Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this twisting exercise that strengthens your obliques. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '100631201', '100631201-Standing-Hands-Up-Twist-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Hands Up Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Hands Up Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad46a014-5e38-4dd6-9e34-e4291e5c9a80', 'Goblet Sumo Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Goblet Sumo Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '75471201', '75471201-Dumbbell-Goblet-Sumo-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Goblet Sumo Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet Sumo Squat', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ad48c0c2-5406-4010-b4fb-2a92064f1603', 'Slight Squat Front Punch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic squatting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '93661201', '93661201-Slight-Squat-Front-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. Perfect for targeting your quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Slight Squat Front Punch', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad4b133b-fe97-4fe7-952c-45c5aa780150', 'Seated Lat Pulldown (Chair, Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Seated Lat Pulldown On A Chair is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '91171201', '91171201-Sitting-Lat-Pulldown-on-a-Chair-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Seated Lat Pulldown On A Chair', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ad4e5e0d-7233-4cd6-9a87-9dd14b422d1d', 'Lying Rear Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '78651201', '78651201-Dumbbell-Lying-Rear-Lateral-Raise-(female)_Shoulde.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lying Rear Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ad554f29-a496-419b-9b30-4670fb247e41', 'Criss Cross Elbow To Knee', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Criss Cross Elbow To Knee builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '47081201', '47081201-Criss-Cross-Elbow-To-Knee_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Criss Cross Elbow To Knee. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Criss Cross Elbow To Knee', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad68c4d2-0960-4bc7-aa53-ee8a9232f456', 'Chest And Front Of Shoulder Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Chest And Front Of Shoulder Stretch is a stretching exercise that targets your chest muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '12711201', '12711201-Chest-and-Front-of-Shoulder-Stretch_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Chest And Front Of Shoulder Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Chest And Front Of Shoulder Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad77e5f0-abaf-4a9c-85fb-a6de80940fe9', 'Seated Leg Curl (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Curl Machine', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '22571201', '22571201-Lever-Seated-Leg-Curl-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Leg Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lever Seated Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('ad92fafb-b386-4408-b793-8313bb03dce2', 'Roll Calves (single Leg)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Roll Calves (single Leg) isolates your calf muscles through a movement motion. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '54391201', '54391201-Roll-Calves-(Single-Leg)-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 2. Set up in the starting position for Roll Calves. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Roll Calves', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ad9c6953-0b35-4ba2-8fbf-170bcd0db6c8', '3 Point Bench Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell 3 Point Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '80031201', '80031201-Dumbbell-3-Point-Bench-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell 3 Point Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', '3 Point Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ada0f803-5467-400e-bc88-303cad8626d4', 'Stepback With Push', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity pushing exercise that challenges your entire body. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '55891201', '55891201-Stepback-with-Push-(Male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Stepback With Push. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Stepback With Push', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ada1984f-3e48-4f61-aee0-56009d1e7fad', 'Bicycle V Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Bicycle V Up, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '78561201', '78561201-Bicycle-V-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bicycle V Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Bicycle V Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ada8ef4a-c366-4a0f-9284-0843b57d197d', 'Pinch Curl (Plate)', 'Arms', 'Weight Plate', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '106361201', '106361201-Weighted-Plate-Pinch-Curl-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. An effective movement for your arms routine.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Weighted Plate Pinch Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('adb1a7b2-8184-4169-baa3-da8e2f68108f', 'Downward Dog Hip Circle', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your hamstrings, calves, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '79001201', '79001201-Downward-Dog-Hip-Circle-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Downward Dog Hip Circle. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Dog Hip Circle', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('adb2c67a-53fb-4cf6-9ff1-a4863bc4003f', 'Thread The Needle Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your upper back area and enhance overall flexibility. The shoulders, thoracic spine assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '59041201', '59041201-Thread-the-Needle-Pose -(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Thread The Needle Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Thread The Needle Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('adc7ca39-a317-482c-9510-c3a79493d9e8', 'Seated Shoulder Shrug', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your shoulders, the Seated Shoulder Shrug helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '81271201', '81271201-Seated-Shoulder-Shrug-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Seated Shoulder Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('add4c5d3-509d-4dba-838c-04d6eb55d456', 'Wide Glute Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This bridging exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '58041201', '58041201-Wide-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. This exercise is excellent for glutes development. Variation: Wide Glute Bridge.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Wide Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('add6a910-747a-4582-81a0-80cac3217237', 'Pin Bench Press Conventional Grip (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '76211201', '76211201-Barbell-Pin-Bench-Press-Conventional-grip-(male)_C.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Pin Bench Press Conventional Grip', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('adda8cea-5eea-4465-8d65-6d43c4b938c8', 'Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Cable Pulldown is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '1981201', '01981201-Cable-Pulldown_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('adf3932b-4b31-484a-8810-6afcf130b0c9', 'Leg To Side', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '9551201', '09551201-Leg-to-Side-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Leg To Side. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Leg To Side', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ae2393f4-3fc5-49a6-97ac-e4fa85450fd6', 'Bench Press - Single Weight (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this pressing exercise for bigger arms. Your chest work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '2961201', '02961201-Dumbbell-Close-grip-Press_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Close Grip Press. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Close Grip Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Press - Close Grip', 'Press - Close Grip', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ae334324-52e8-4589-9293-793bc5281bd3', 'Rear Lunge (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '781201', '00781201-Barbell-Rear-Lunge_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Rear Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Rear Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('ae40ba47-6ed3-43f6-9135-02a9a917e66f', 'Standing Triple Arm Cross', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Standing Triple Arm Cross, an effective movement movement for upper body strength. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '94311201', '94311201-Standing-Triple-Arm-Cross-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Triple Arm Cross. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Triple Arm Cross', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ae478662-c9eb-4d4b-9ffd-75160d628e50', 'Slight Squat Front Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '90511201', '90511201-Slight-Squat-Front-Raise-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Slight Squat Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ae63a880-b339-447c-b218-7e30f8c9d772', 'Standing Contralateral Chest Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '98151201', '98151201-Cable-Standing-Contralateral-Chest-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Contralateral Chest Press. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Standing Contralateral Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ae645608-3bba-44a8-8a61-58342e1812f0', 'Seated Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Seated Lateral Raise is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '3951201', '03951201-Dumbbell-Seated-Lateral-Raise_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Lateral Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Seated Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ae76abab-e074-45ad-a1ec-4b1b8ef2e492', 'Standing Balance Side To Front Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Standing Balance Side To Front Leg Raise is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '77061201', '77061201-Standing-Balance-Side-to-Front-Leg-Raise-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Standing Balance Side To Front Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ae7e1251-d1d7-488b-bb14-c5a7742c977c', 'Torso Twist In Plank On Elbows Position', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Torso Twist In Plank On Elbows Position is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '104191201', '104191201-Torso-Twist-in-Plank-on-Elbows-Position-(male)_Wa.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Torso Twist In Plank On Elbows Position', 'crunch, leg_raise, russian_twist, dead_bug', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ae7eae2c-9cc8-4711-b30c-88e6cc5928c0', 'Duck And Side Punch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '58521201', '58521201-Duck-and-Side-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Duck And Side Punch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Duck And Side Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aea88516-fe17-4637-820c-c9633a021275', 'Bent Over Kickback With Rope Attachment - Neutral Grip (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this kicking exercise for bigger arms. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '45781201', '45781201-Cable-Bent-Over-Neutral-Grip-Kickback-with-Rope-Attachment_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Bent Over Neutral Grip Kickback With Rope Attachment. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 4. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 5. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Bent Over Kickback With Rope Attachment - Neutral Grip', 'Bent Over Kickback With Rope Attachment - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('aeb45ef3-45e3-40ab-ada1-719d49551bcd', 'Sleeping Swan Yoga Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '78381201', '78381201-Sleeping-Swan-Yoga-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Sleeping Swan Yoga Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Sleeping Swan Yoga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aebbf3ad-f1f5-489b-a3b2-3d7f8510f6bf', 'Lean Back Tap Ankle Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lean Back Tap Ankle Tap is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '88551201', '88551201-Lean-Back-Tap-Ankle-Tap-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Lean Back Tap Ankle Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lean Back Tap Ankle Tap', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aec9c2ca-9914-4a43-b7a9-070d766a6c29', 'Chest Press (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Chest', 'Chest Press Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '24561201', '24561201-Lever-Chest-Press-(plate-loaded)-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('aed50eff-0164-4455-aad3-0cd108f4f76e', 'Incline Plyo Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '90641201', '90641201-Incline-Plyo-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 73, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Incline Plyo Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aee1e5ae-cdd2-452b-9701-e8725f8c189b', 'Kickback (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this kicking exercise for bigger arms. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '24371201', '24371201-Dumbbell-Kickback-(female)_Upper-arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Kickback', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('aee59d22-50a2-4c29-afb5-09191b3ac94a', '3/4 Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The 3/4 Sit Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '24761201', '24761201-3-4-Sit-up-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for 3 4 Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', 'Trunk Flexion', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', '3/4 Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aee954e3-b322-4e6f-ab12-17c0b66c673a', 'Vertical Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lever Vertical Leg Press is a pressing exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '83681201', '83681201-Lever-Vertical-Leg-Press-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Vertical Leg Press. 2. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 3. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Vertical Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('aee9f092-525b-44fd-b8ee-0b7a9f461d65', 'Sit Up To Press (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Sit Up To Press is a core pressing exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '93361201', '93361201-Dumbbell-Sit-up-to-Press-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Sit Up To Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Sit Up To Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Sit Up To Press', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('aeea6e17-3826-48cc-ac38-727773079ed7', 'Seated Crunch Chest Pad (Machine)', 'Core', 'Ab Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '5951201', '05951201-Lever-Seated-Crunch-(chest-pad).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Crunch. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lever Seated Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('aeeb9cfa-4ae2-49bd-af78-0c96726c2048', 'Standing Military Press', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '43461201', '43461201-Bodyweight-Standing-Military-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Standing Military Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aef38acf-7752-4a5a-9d87-b8498ad837cd', 'Tate Press (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Tate Press targets your triceps through a pressing motion. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '4361201', '04361201-Dumbbell-Tate-Press_Triceps.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Tate Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Tate Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Tate Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('af070cc0-82ff-486c-a7cd-272f31ab4018', 'Side Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Side Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '7081201', '07081201-Side-Crunch_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. An effective movement for your core routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Side Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af18176e-861f-4a72-8a93-49268ac78c31', 'Seated Deep Neck Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your neck area and enhance overall flexibility. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '81291201', '81291201-Seated-Deep-Neck-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Deep Neck Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Deep Neck Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af18df9f-f972-47cf-a29b-4cd9e1451f83', 'Knee Touch Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Knee Touch Crunch, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '42691201', '42691201-Knee-Touch-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Works well for abs activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Knee Touch Crunch', 'crunch, plank, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af1d2c74-7e61-47b4-8b0d-92e77f6ad153', 'Russian Twist Legs Side Waves', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Russian Twist Legs Side Waves. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '105841201', '105841201-Russian-Twist-Legs-Side-Waves-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Russian Twist Legs Side Waves. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Russian Twist Legs Side Waves', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af480ffd-4651-4937-9208-97922a2ad2b7', 'Standing Y Raise (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '88991201', '88991201-Cable-Standing-Y-raise-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Y Raise. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Cable Standing Y Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Standing Y Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('af4a0939-6129-47cb-963c-e0d9fe723528', 'Bench Press - Neutral Grip (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Neutral Grip Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '66201201', '66201201-Kettlebell-Neutral-grip-Bench-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Neutral Grip Bench Press. 2. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Bench Press - Neutral Grip', 'Bench Press - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('af4d3b7c-3f53-49f7-9893-4c316fb58643', 'Roll Posterior Shoulder Lying On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Roll Posterior Shoulder Lying On Floor is a movement exercise that targets your core for shoulder development. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '54181201', '54181201-Roll-Posterior-Shoulder-Lying-on-Floor-(female)_Sh.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Posterior Shoulder Lying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Roll Posterior Shoulder Lying On Floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Roll Posterior Shoulder Lying On Floor', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af5f6ab4-6191-490a-b3b2-d30fb4a44012', 'Bench Press (Smith Machine)', 'Chest', 'Smith Machine, Flat Bench', '{Pectorals}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '70021201', '70021201-Smith-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Great for building strength in your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Smith Bench Press', 'Bench Press', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('af615db9-d383-49ef-a2d0-cd08e1870ca9', 'Knees And Toes Point Out Squat Slide Wall (Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '89551201', '89551201-Knees-and-Toes-Point-Out-Squat-Slide-Wall-(male)_H.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Knees And Toes Point Out Squat Slide Wall', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af6371a1-9078-45f1-92ee-266edca37e0f', 'Squat To Jumping Jack', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Squat To Jumping Jack builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your shoulders, calves working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '78251201', '78251201-Squat-to-Jumping-Jack-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Explode upward from the bottom, jumping as high as possible. 4. Land softly with bent knees and immediately descend into the next rep. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Squat To Jumping Jack', 'burpee, high_knees, jump_rope', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af6b00f4-b165-4832-b295-539379750933', 'Elbow Lift Reverse Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pushing movement targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '70761201', '70761201-Elbow-Lift-Reverse-Push-Up-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. A solid choice for back day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Elbow Lift Reverse Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af96b1e3-2a1c-4c65-aced-2a6f9725cba2', 'Quadruped To Down Dog', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Quadruped To Down Dog helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '82511201', '82511201-Quadruped-to-Down-Dog-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Quadruped To Down Dog. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Quadruped To Down Dog', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('af9accc2-0f86-4a4c-a267-732d251959f0', 'Quadriceps Lying Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '9391201', '09391201-Quadriceps-lying-stretch-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Quadriceps Lying Stretch. 2. Move into the stretch position for Quadriceps Lying Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. A solid choice for stretching day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Quadriceps Lying Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('afa28396-fe78-4726-b445-7048b3139fb0', 'Bent Over Wide Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '93991201', '93991201-Dumbbell-Bent-Over-Wide-Row-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bent Over Wide Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'general_exercise', 'Bent Over Wide Row', 'lat_pulldown, pull_up, bicep_curl, face_pull, seated_row', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('afb02197-b4d5-47f0-94b9-ce464492d3ea', 'Kneeling Triceps Kickback (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Lower Chest"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Kneeling Triceps Kickback is an arm kicking exercise targeting your glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '78801201', '78801201-Dumbbell-Kneeling-Triceps-Kickback-(female)_Upper-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Kneeling Triceps Kickback. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 4. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Kneeling Triceps Kickback', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('afb28a8d-3a16-4d1d-bc07-252f93127c13', 'Decline Chest Fly (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '25121201', '25121201-Cable-Decline-Fly-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Decline Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Fly', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Decline Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('afb33c65-1507-4f5e-b5e3-04cca3027764', 'Single Leg Deadlift Pass (Kettlebell)', 'Back', 'Kettlebell', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Single Leg Deadlift Pass is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '105611201', '105611201-Kettlebell-Single-Leg-Deadlift-Pass_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Single Leg Deadlift Pass. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'deadlift', 'Single Leg Deadlift Pass', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('afd96945-33ab-4bba-849b-081e1a083f22', 'Row - Close Grip (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Band Close Grip Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '70471201', '70471201-Band-Close-Grip-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Close Grip Row. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Pull', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, 'Neutral', 'Standard', 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Row - Close Grip', 'Row - Close Grip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('afed4803-247e-4f0c-b641-9c6b0812e134', 'Kneeling Iliopsoas Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '67711201', '67711201-Kneeling-Iliopsoas-Stretch-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Iliopsoas Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Kneeling Iliopsoas Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aff316da-20b3-4ecb-8d63-a02ebce47eed', 'Wide Stance Side Lunge (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'This lunging movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '86561201', '86561201-Wide-Stance-Side-Lunge-against-Wall-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Wide Stance Side Lunge Against Wall', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('aff7876e-8d1c-4fba-92b1-cd74d5bc7b48', 'Rotate And Leg Lift Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Rotate And Leg Lift Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '71521201', '71521201-Rotate-and-Leg-Lift-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. This variation specifically emphasizes the abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Rotate And Leg Lift Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b02f2d10-1be3-480a-aa26-78128898f53d', 'Standing Single Arm Horizontal Triceps Extension (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This full-body movement exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '86141201', '86141201-Cable-Standing-Single-Arm-Horizontal-Triceps-Exten.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Single Arm Horizontal Triceps Exten. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Standing Single Arm Horizontal Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b033ff31-f276-4dfe-8148-b372c2f1f2d1', 'Leg Curl (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. Secondary activation of your calves provides additional muscle engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '24221201', '24221201-Resistance-Band-Leg-Curl-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Leg Curl. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('b0438bd5-75cc-49d2-b7e3-b4a087cef971', 'Lying Hip Lift (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '6181201', '06181201-Lying-Hip-Lift-(on-stability-ball)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Lying Hip Lift. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Hip Lift. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. Include this in your legs training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Lying Hip Lift', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b054b861-be6c-40b7-9559-2b7beedfd09d', 'Seated Leg Extension (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Cable Seated Leg Extension is a extension exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '56641201', '56641201-Cable-Seated-Leg-Extension_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Leg Extension. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 4. Lower with control back to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Seated Leg Extension', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b06b39d9-9104-486c-b853-efe144c1f931', 'Chin To Chest Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '2521201', '02521201-Chin-to-chest-Stretch-(female)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Chin To Chest Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Chin To Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b073ed33-9faa-4906-b939-5a69fd3e1182', 'Neck Circle Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Neck Circle Stretch provides a deep stretch for your neck, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '42761201', '42761201-Neck-Circle-Stretch-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Neck Circle Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Neck Circle Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b073fea8-06b9-4a36-9b85-e15f55d5df71', 'Weighted Front Raise Hold', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your front delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '75881201', '75881201-Weighted-Front-Raise-Hold_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Weighted Front Raise Hold', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b08def3c-c22c-4b55-8b06-e0a66d38c0b8', 'Seated Bent Arm Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '70211201', '70211201-Dumbbell-Seated-Bent-Arm-Lateral-Raise-(female)_Sh.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Bent Arm Lateral Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Seated Bent Arm Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b09c64b2-208f-4d02-8608-114733a82ca4', 'Spider Mountain Climber', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This dynamic climbing movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors, shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '74631201', '74631201-Spider-Mountain-Climber-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 2. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 3. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Spider Mountain Climber', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b0a17e06-245b-4f63-809f-1bdefb029734', 'Overhead Jack To Jumping Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Calves"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Overhead Jack To Jumping Jack builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The shoulders, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '45511201', '45511201-Overhead-Jack-To-Jumping-Jack_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Overhead Jack To Jumping Jack. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Overhead Jack To Jumping Jack', 'burpee, high_knees, jump_rope', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b0aa252f-8cc2-4ee9-b11e-151a85340ee4', 'Standing Torso Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this twisting exercise that strengthens your obliques. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '73551201', '73551201-Standing-Torso-Twist-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Torso Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Torso Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b0aa83cf-30d1-4c15-8bda-2c93f93cfab0', 'Lying Lifting On Hip (Barbell)', 'Core', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Lying Lifting (on Hip) is a lower body movement exercise that targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '581201', '00581201-Barbell-Lying-Lifting-(On-Hip)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Lying Lifting. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Barbell Lying Lifting. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 54, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Lying Lifting', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b0ac6b96-45c9-4675-ab34-8eb03636f95a', 'Glute Bridge And Double Open Up', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '94431201', '94431201-Glute-Bridge-and-Double-Open-up-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability. An effective movement for your legs routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge And Double Open Up', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b0b110d5-5cab-468e-9a43-50de9a43f5b9', 'Glute Ham Developer Sit Up And Russian Twist (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Ab Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Glute Ham Developer Sit Up And Russian Twist targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '47631201', '47631201-Glute-Ham-Developer-Sit-up-and-Russian-Twist_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Glute Ham Developer Sit Up And Russian Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Glute Ham Developer Sit Up And Russian Twist', 'crunch, leg_raise, plank', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b0b14d68-ff23-486c-a54c-f3b68279b245', 'Romanian Deadlift To Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Romanian Deadlift To Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '94851201', '94851201-Kettlebell-Romanian-Deadlift-to-Squat-(male)_Thigh.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Romanian Deadlift To Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift To Squat', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('b0b67643-799b-4d8b-a81b-a2fff3a4ccde', 'Burpee Shuffle', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'The Burpee Shuffle is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. Secondary activation of your chest, quads provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '59311201', '59311201-Burpee-Shuffle-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Burpee Shuffle', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b0ba51d7-8548-4f6d-a68a-8f3c208f0f20', 'Floor Fly (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Kettlebell Floor Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '58581201', '58581201-Kettlebell-Floor-Fly_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Floor Fly. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Kettlebell Floor Fly. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Floor Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('b0bcab3b-b018-4fb3-855b-74cdc4eee999', 'Lying Hip Flexion Reverse Squat (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '88761201', '88761201-Cable-Lying-Hip-Flexion-(Reverse-Squat)-(male)_Hip.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Hip Flexion. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Hip Flexion. 3. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 4. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 5. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Lying Hip Flexion', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b0cd7359-5adb-4ac0-b878-2b65da984c50', 'Curl To Press (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '107281201', '107281201-Band-Curl-to-Press-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Curl To Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Curl To Press', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('b0e3b177-80ca-4e60-9b12-b5b0a60321a8', 'Hands Behind Head Chest Squeeze', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Hands Behind Head Chest Squeeze, an effective movement movement for upper body strength. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '59921201', '59921201-Hands-Behind-Head-Chest-Squeeze-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hands Behind Head Chest Squeeze. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Hands Behind Head Chest Squeeze', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b0f93322-0218-417f-8e2a-f14770d3779d', 'Lateral to Front Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your lateral delts with the Dumbbell Lateral To Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '3351201', '03351201-Dumbbell-Lateral-to-Front-Raise_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lateral To Front Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Lateral To Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b11f8143-2c9b-4b44-8cb0-06cb86d15f0b', 'Kneeling Push Up To Hovering Table Top (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Chest', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Push Up To Hovering Table Top is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '89731201', '89731201-Kneeling-Push-Up-to-Hovering-Table-Top-(male)_Ches.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Kneeling Push Up To Hovering Table Top', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('b1270ff0-7245-4398-8d0d-87aa1641a09b', 'Leg Climb Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Leg Climb Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '69431201', '69431201-Leg-Climb-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. A solid choice for core day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Leg Climb Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b12ae019-889c-4d09-94d6-09c09f54df0f', 'Hand Swipe March', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Hand Swipe March is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '84561201', '84561201-Hand-Swipe-March-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hand Swipe March. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Hand Swipe March', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b130b5b7-e1b0-451c-98b8-ff69c03716df', 'Downward Dog Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Downward Dog Crunch, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '81831201', '81831201-Downward-Dog-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Dog Crunch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b131a377-ce10-4104-a2b5-65b8fac32bc7', '90 Degree Heel Touch (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The 90 Degree Heel Touch Against Wall is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '74361201', '74361201-90-Degree-Heel-Touch-against-Wall-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for 90 Degree Heel Touch Against Wall. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', '90 Degree Heel Touch Against Wall', 'crunch, bicycle_crunch, russian_twist', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1394a99-a671-434c-b18b-c42cca2ef0df', 'Hip Abduction (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Hip Abduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your glute med/abductors. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '10771201', '10771201-Suspender-Hip-Abduction-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Hip Abduction. 2. Set up in the starting position for Suspender Hip Abduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Suspender Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('b144793e-33c2-4118-b6bb-482b6df1632a', 'Low To High Lunge Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your quads, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79691201', '79691201-Low-to-High-Lunge-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Low To High Lunge Pose. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 70, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Low To High Lunge Pose', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b160de45-fe3b-442f-a42a-330d890a588b', 'Assisted Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '44431201', '44431201-Dumbbell-Assisted-Bulgarian-Split-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Assisted Bulgarian Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Assisted Bulgarian Split Squat', 'split_squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b16a283d-18db-40dd-aef0-136b676d5641', 'Standing Single Arm Hammer Curl With Rope Attack (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing One Arm Hammer Curl With Rope Attac is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '53701201', '53701201-Cable-Standing-One-Arm-Hammer-Curl-with-Rope-Attac.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing One Arm Hammer Curl With Rope Attac. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 4. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 5. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 6. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 7. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 8. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hammer_curl', 'Standing Single Arm Hammer Curl With Rope Attack', 'bicep_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b16ac909-8d91-4d4e-86ab-b2b710d036d1', 'Goblet Side Lunge Stretch (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Goblet Side Lunge Stretch provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '93011201', '93011201-Dumbbell-Goblet-Side-Lunge-Stretch-(VERSION-2)-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Goblet Side Lunge Stretch. 2. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 72, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Goblet Side Lunge Stretch', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b17c6437-e414-43fb-aeba-efa2805d5411', 'Standing Hands On Shoulder Raise And Elbow Touch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The obliques assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '96301201', '96301201-Standing-Hands-On-Shoulder-Raise-and-Elbow-Touch-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Standing Hands On Shoulder Raise And Elbow Touch (. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Standing Hands On Shoulder Raise And Elbow Touch (', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1810944-6777-49f1-9d14-c65bc31486ef', 'Side Lunge Wood Chop', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this lunging exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '68591201', '68591201-Side-Lunge-Wood-Chop-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Perfect for targeting your obliques.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Side Lunge Wood Chop', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1960ddc-28d8-4b78-b8ce-c5c452667206', 'Seated Shoulder Press (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Shoulder Press On A Chair is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '90971201', '90971201-Sitting-Shoulder-Press-on-a-Chair-(female)_Shoulde.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press On A Chair', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1b89a16-62e8-4019-a1f7-38851cb43a8f', '90 To 90 (Leaning)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '77671201', '77671201-90-to-90-Lean-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for 90 To 90 Lean. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', 'Static / Mobility', 'Static', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', '90 To 90', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1cb7d76-17a8-4ea9-a28d-0b4f6381d40f', 'Sit Up II', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '7351201', '07351201-Sit-Up-II_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sit Up II. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Sit Up II', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1cfa545-0260-476f-b35e-cf328d997b09', 'Single Arm Upright Row (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rowing movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your traps working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '26001201', '26001201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Upright-Row-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 3. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'upright_row', 'Single Arm Upright Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b1e0b594-e1ec-4eda-a97b-c70459ff3284', 'Sumo High Pull (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Sumo High Pull is a pulling exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Secondary activation of your adductors, glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '5481201', '05481201-Kettlebell-Sumo-High-Pull_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Sumo High Pull. 2. Set up in the starting position for Kettlebell Sumo High Pull. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'upright_row', 'Sumo High Pull', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('b1e29896-4f92-4b56-83ed-0ce00fd4b580', 'Seated Single Leg Hugging Knee Flexion', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this flexion movement focusing on your core. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '105411201', '105411201-Seated-Single-Leg-Hugging-Knee-Flexion-(male)_Thi.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Seated Single Leg Hugging Knee Flexion', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1ecda42-ce2a-4181-997e-d93f1870111e', 'Lying Single Toe Pointing', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted movement exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '64101201', '64101201-Lying-Single-Toe-Pointing-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Single Toe Pointing. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Single Toe Pointing. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Single Toe Pointing', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1fe3847-1e79-4ef6-b430-5de18b04f83b', 'Standing Figure Four Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Standing Figure Four Pose provides a deep stretch for your glutes, ideal for recovery and mobility work. You''ll also feel your hips working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '59021201', '59021201-Standing-Figure-Four-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Figure Four Pose. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 52, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Standing Figure Four Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b1fe7c2d-bcaa-4995-a299-e8515cd706b7', 'Inverted Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Your biceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '22991201', '22991201-Inverted-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Inverted Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b21e9164-a840-42ed-a3c4-82334e797c37', 'Forward Fold Twist With Toe Hold', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your hamstrings, the Forward Fold Twist With Toe Hold helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your lower back, calves working to support the movement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79031201', '79031201-Forward-Fold-Twist-with-Toe-Hold-(female)_Stretchi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Forward Fold Twist With Toe Hold. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Move into the stretch position for Forward Fold Twist With Toe Hold. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Forward Fold Twist With Toe Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b221f701-3e65-4e1f-848d-7da5d1848590', 'Gate Rock (advanced)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase. Listen to your body and adjust intensity as needed.', '88701201', '88701201-Gate-Rock-(advanced)-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Gate Rock. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dynamic_warmup', 'Gate Rock', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b23b88fa-2286-4909-80e3-00eefbcc2269', 'Inverted Row Bent Knee Under Table', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '33821201', '33821201-Inverted-Row-Bent-Knee-under-Table-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. A solid choice for back day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Inverted Row Bent Knee Under Table', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b246c2ed-d45d-4733-856e-0095ce5600cb', 'Pushdown Straight Arm (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pushing movement targeting your triceps. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '1991201', '01991201-Cable-Pushdown-(straight-arm)-(VERSION-2)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b24d64da-0ba5-4b0e-ab03-ead04cbdcf2c', 'Landmine Overhead Rear Lunge (Landmine)', 'Legs', 'Landmine Attachment, Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Landmine Overhead Rear Lunge is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '76271201', '76271201-Landmine-Overhead-Rear-Lunge_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Landmine Overhead Rear Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b266ee24-5d72-4533-bc05-3489c35603f0', 'Spine Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this twisting exercise that strengthens your obliques. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '23291201', '23291201-Spine-Twist_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Spine Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Spine Twist', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b26c9186-d77a-419c-a7ca-aa6c91a13dc4', 'Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Romanian Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '851201', '00851201-Barbell-Romanian-Deadlift_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Romanian Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Hip Hinge', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b26dc2f1-323e-44ad-8275-ef4aa8a965bf', 'Standing March With Shoulders Extension', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this extension exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '53601201', '53601201-Standing-March-with-Shoulders-Extension-(female)_P.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Extend through the target joint(s) for Standing March With Shoulders Extension. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Standing March With Shoulders Extension', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b27499bf-8c05-46de-b268-d5003815a53f', 'Standing Diagonal Prayer Push - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Standing Alternating Diagonal Prayer Push, a comprehensive pushing exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '94721201', '94721201-Standing-Alternating-Diagonal-Prayer-Push-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Diagonal Prayer Push - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b275b5cf-f9d5-45f0-8812-3eba4765ac0b', 'Shin Box Switch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '46081201', '46081201-Shin-Box-Switch_Stretching.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Move into the stretch position for Shin Box Switch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Shin Box Switch', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b27ceefb-2938-4fcd-a556-db8d205f6ec4', 'Thomas Test', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Thomas Test provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '67941201', '67941201-Thomas-Test-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Thomas Test. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Thomas Test', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b28b48b5-ea3d-4a18-8704-a9e5acfa4231', 'Lying Upper Body T Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this raising movement targeting your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '95511201', '95511201-Lying-Upper-Body-T-Raise-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Upper Body T Raise. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Upper Body T Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lying Upper Body T Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b290b381-787d-4da0-bcbd-2c145ea747e1', 'Triceps Extension Stepback', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Triceps Extension Stepback is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic extension movements. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '85791201', '85791201-Triceps-Extension-Stepback-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Triceps Extension Stepback', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b2a7dafc-c670-4aa8-bc00-3ef9b54b3b1a', 'Kneeling Bend Knee (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '105431201', '105431201-Kneeling-Bend-Knee-Chair-Supported-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Bend Knee Chair Supported', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b2bcc9aa-d0e5-4a50-b22d-30bd5e3783ac', 'Circle Arms Knee Raise (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this raising exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '66361201', '66361201-Circle-Arms-Knee-Raises-on-Chair-(male)_Plyometric.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Circle Arms Knee Raises On Chair. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Circle Arms Knee Raise On Chair', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b2c820ac-c1b1-4223-b519-a7eb87417019', 'Calf Raise With Wall Support (Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Calf Raise With Wall Support isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '52571201', '52571201-Calf-Raise-with-Wall-Support-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 3. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 4. Lower with control and repeat. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Calf Raise With Wall Support', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b2e33479-669a-4b84-9c9b-15273603c627', 'Standing Single Leg Curl (Plate Loaded)', 'Legs', 'Leg Curl Machine', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Lever Standing Single Leg Curl (plate Loaded) targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '107211201', '107211201-Lever-Standing-Single-Leg-Curl-(plate-loaded)-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Single Leg Curl. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lever Standing Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b2e7ed32-a199-4315-a07b-ee13079b9c86', 'Lying Triceps Extension (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '26921201', '26921201-Barbell-Lying-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Lying Triceps Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Barbell Lying Triceps Extension. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b2f2aa9b-cd2a-4713-a258-97d9c1063fed', 'Heel Glute Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '64351201', '64351201-Heel-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. Beneficial for overall legs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Heel Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b304c00a-e4b0-464c-8a48-2f5ac9adbe22', 'Standing Ladder Climb', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Standing Ladder Climb builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '85551201', '85551201-Standing-Ladder-Climb-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Ladder Climb. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Ladder Climb', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b313ca0b-58cc-47ac-b0c0-ef759746d4c0', 'Half Jackknife', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Half Jackknife is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '73321201', '73321201-Half-Jackknife-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Half Jackknife. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'v_up', 'Half Jackknife', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b31b0a1d-16f8-44bb-b622-8cd3cdc7e1e9', 'Triceps Dip Floor (Dip Bars)', 'Arms', 'Dip Bars', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Triceps Dip Floor targets your triceps through a dipping motion. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '8151201', '08151201-Triceps-Dip-Floor_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Triceps Dip Floor. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Triceps Dip Floor', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b31e6d8c-0d4d-4b50-abdb-bf3f09311d0f', 'Standing Romanian Deadlift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '65721201', '65721201-Bodyweight-Standing-Romanian-Deadlift-(female)_Hip.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Standing Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b327fd08-78cd-4378-b1e3-0563707a6763', 'Standing Pulldown Rope (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Pulldown (with Rope) is an arm pulling exercise targeting your lats. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '2321201', '02321201-Cable-Standing-Pulldown-(with-rope)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Pulldown. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 54, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Standing Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b32e3b49-857d-4d52-a575-fa152a41d7aa', 'Side Mountain Climber', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Mountain Climber is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. Secondary activation of your hip flexors, shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '56801201', '56801201-Side-Mountain-Climber-(male)_Cardio_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 2. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 3. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Side Mountain Climber', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b333deab-330c-44d4-9531-c48c1b1b64bb', 'Weighted Lying Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Weighted Lying Twist. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '8391201', '08391201-Weighted-Lying-Twist-(female)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Lying Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Weighted Lying Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Weighted Lying Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b34eca5f-44ad-4c71-b991-3cdf3583be10', 'Knees And Toes Point Out Squat Slide Wall (Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '87711201', '87711201-Knees-and-Toes-Point-Out-Squat-Slide-Wall-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement. An effective movement for your legs routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Knees And Toes Point Out Squat Slide Wall', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b3582aec-e12a-459a-8231-b43b99cfad22', 'Seated Wrist Curl (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The EZ Bar Seated Wrist Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '55791201', '55791201-EZ-Bar-Seated-Wrist-Curl_Forearms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Grip the EZ bar on the angled portions for a comfortable wrist position. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'EZ Bar Seated Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b3592b98-5c2b-4c76-b9af-17b7b5370661', 'Chest Supported Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Chest Supported Lateral Raises is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '36851201', '36851201-Dumbbell-Chest-Supported-Lateral-Raises_Shoulders-.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Chest Supported Lateral Raises. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Chest Supported Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90);
